# Implementation Plan — Benin Tech Fest 2.0 Redesign

This plan outlines the design and structural enhancements to be made to the Benin Tech Fest 2.0 landing page. The goal is to break away from traditional, flat corporate layouts and elevate the website into a high-octane, premium, and elite tech movement that visually signals the scale of the event (now merged with **Edo Startup Week** and expanded to a 4-day event).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Font Transition**: We are replacing the standard Google Fonts (like `Righteous` and `Geologica`) with **Cabinet Grotesk** (visuals and main headings) and **Oswald** (sub-headings).
> - **Color Scheme Re-mapping**: We will change the dominant theme accent from Red (`#b91c1c` / `var(--signal-red)`) to the premium vibrant Blue (`#007cf9`), keeping Red (`#ff0000` / `#b91c1c`) as a recessive accent color reserved strictly for key focal points.
> - **Cultural Rooting**: We will introduce sharp geometric grids, glowing network lines, and digital architectural lines that evoke Benin's historic legacy of elite craftsmanship (bronze casting, structural carving) translated into high-tech design patterns.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Typography Integration & Theme Mapping
We will integrate **Cabinet Grotesk** via Fontshare and clean up the typography system to ensure the hierarchy matches the design doc.

#### [MODIFY] [globals.css](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/app/globals.css)
- Import Cabinet Grotesk using the Fontshare API:
  `@import url('https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=cabinet-grotesk@400,500,700,800,900&display=swap');`
- Re-configure `@theme` to define `--font-cabinet-grotesk` and map `--font-righteous` (or a new `--font-cabinet`) to it so that it immediately propagates to all main visual headings without breaking the existing codebase.
- Re-configure `--font-oswald` as the primary sub-typeface.

#### [MODIFY] [layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/app/layout.tsx)
- Keep google font `Oswald` and base readability font `Andika`. Remove/clean up unused google fonts if they aren't needed to optimize performance.

---

### 2. Color Scheme Shift (Vibrant Blue Dominance & Recessive Red)
We will align the color vars so that `#007cf9` is the hero and `#ff0000` is kept for key visual points.

#### [MODIFY] [globals.css](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/app/globals.css)
- Modify `:root` variables:
  ```css
  --brand-blue: #007cf9;
  --brand-red: #ff0000;
  --color-highlight-yellow: var(--brand-blue); /* Map highlight color to brand blue */
  --color-brand-red: var(--brand-red);
  ```
- Ensure the glowing ambient animations (`Global3DBackground.tsx` and custom gradients) reflect this color hierarchy, using more blue atmosphere and reserving red for small, high-frequency focal points.

---

### 3. Messaging: Convergence, Scale, & The Edo Startup Week Merger
Since Benin Tech Fest has merged with Edo Startup Week and expanded to 4 days, the hero text and layout need to convey this scale.

#### [MODIFY] [Hero.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/app/components/Hero.tsx)
- Add a prominent, sleek, glowing badge/banner: **"Benin Tech Fest × Edo Startup Week • Merged & Expanded to 4 Days"**.
- Update dates and details to reflect the 4-day span clearly.
- Adjust button colors and highlight elements to use `#007cf9` as the primary action and keep the red/white accents for the secondary elements.

#### [MODIFY] [About.tsx](file:///c:/Users/ohioa/Projects/React/benin-tech-fest/app/components/About.tsx)
- Update text content to explicitly mention:
  > *"Benin Tech Fest 2.0 has merged with Edo Startup Week, expanding into a massive 4-day convergence. It is Edo State's premier tech festival..."*
- Add an overlapping geometric pattern to the side image to symbolize locking/uniting the ecosystem.

